        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): dripping model pulls hang past idle timeout during setup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where OpenClaw Ollama setup could hang forever while downloading a model when `/api/pull` kept sending occasional NDJSON progress lines that never advanced `completed`.\n\nAffected workflow: Ollama provider setup / `ensureOllamaModelPulled` model download.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOllama setup already aborts if headers never arrive (30s) and already fails if the pull stream goes fully idle (300s). After headers return, that response timer was cleared, so only the per-chunk idle timer remained. Idle resets on every chunk, so a slow drip can keep the download alive indefinitely.\n\nThis keeps the headers and byte-idle budgets as-is, then arms a **no-progress watchdog** after the first body chunk. The watchdog resets when aggregate Ollama `completed` increases **or when a never-before-seen status text appears**, so:\n- non-advancing drips fail closed\n- advancing large/slow downloads may continue past any fixed wall-clock lifetime\n- healthy post-download finalization phases (first-time \"verifying sha256 digest\", \"writing manifest\", etc.) are not aborted\n- cycling status values without completed progress cannot act as an unlimited keepalive\n\nOptional `streamNoProgressTimeoutMs` / `streamIdleTimeoutMs` on `ensureOllamaModelPulled` are for tests only.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDuring Ollama setup, a wedged or maliciously dripping /api/pull stream fails closed with a no-progress error. Healthy pulls that keep advancing completed or transition through documented status-only finalization survive. True idle stalls still fail at 300s. Cycling status without completed progress is bounded.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `0ffcb1caa29`\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/ollama/src/setup.test.ts extensions/ollama/src/setup.pull.test.ts extensions/ollama/src/setup.pull-deadline.loopback.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```text\n Test Files  3 passed (3)\n      Tests  45 passed (45)\n```\n\nCoverage:\n- existing idle-stall regression (empty body; no-progress not armed)\n- fake-timer non-advancing drip fails with no-progress message\n- fake-timer advancing completed continues past several shortened no-progress windows\n- **NEW** fake-timer status-only finalization (distinct phases) survives past shortened watchdog\n- **NEW** fake-timer cycling status without completed progress aborts within watchdog budget\n- loopback negative idle control: drip + idle stays unsettled\n- loopback non-advancing control: rejects with no-progress\n- **NEW** loopback status-only finalization survives past 100ms budget\n- **NEW** loopback cycling status aborts within 250ms budget\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Cursor).",
